  "question": {
    "text": "A right triangular plate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is free to rotate in the vertical plane about a fixed horizontal axis through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. It is supported by a string such that the side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is horizontal. The reaction at the support <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0031602_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 192px; height: 186px;\" />",
